# No Code-Block Nesting

Keep assistant output clean and easy to scan in the terminal and chat UI.

## Requirements

- Do not nest fenced code blocks inside other fenced code blocks.
- Do not put markdown code fences inside examples that are themselves inside a code fence.
- Prefer separate blocks, bullet lists, or inline backticks when showing nested syntax.
- When documenting file formats (e.g. `.mdc` frontmatter), use indentation or a single outer fence with language `text`/`markdown` and describe inner fences in prose instead of literal nesting.

## Examples

Bad: a markdown tutorial inside a markdown code fence that also contains triple-backtick examples.

Good: one fence per snippet; use "inner fence omitted" or show the inner part in a second standalone block below.
